ce without naming Mutation/_VALID_COMBINATIONS as the thing extended","The preceding architecture story that 'decided the contract' is not visible in this plan text, so whether the union subsumes or duplicates Mutation is ambiguous rather than assertably wrong (COACH, not ASSERT)"],"finding":"AC1's new 'named payload type for every direction/action pair' with construction-time field validation overlaps the existing mutation.py machinery (the frozen Mutation value object plus the _VALID_COMBINATIONS allowlist, which already rejects invalid (direction,action) pairs and validates target/payload/provenance types in __post_init__). The plan does not state how the new typed union relates to Mutation — whether it wraps, replaces, or sits beside it — creating an NIH / premature-abstraction risk that a parallel validation surface is built next to one that already exists.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f925481976055f9c9","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria line 1; Approach bullet 1 ('Introduce the approved direction/action payload union')","norm_id":"n3da48a92095e4ecc","priority":0.033,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/implementer builds a second field-validation layer that duplicates _VALID_COMBINATIONS' pair-rejection, drifting from the single source of truth typed_dispatch._build_leaves already consumes"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Add a plan sentence pinning the payload union to reuse mutation._VALID_COMBINATIONS as the pair-validity source of truth, layering only the new per-action field checks (missing/extra/wrong-action) that Mutation's untyped payload does not currently enforce.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"no","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no",